{=============================================================================
  Brine-to-water heat pump reference model - runnable variant
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0078
  (variant of brine_to_water_heat_pump_refsim.eescode, which is kept in valid
   EES and is blocked in CoolSolve; see its header)
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Faithful runnable transcription of the native file. It changes ONLY what the
  registered CoolSolve gaps force:

  1. CS-GAP-ELSEIF-CHAIN, CS-GAP-UPPERCASE and CS-GAP-STRING-ARRAY break the
     BRINEPROP procedure of the BrineProp library
     (EES "ELSE IF" chains closed by repeated "ENDIF", the string function
     Uppercase$, string arrays read by index). It is split in two, as in CSL-0072:
     - a selector PROCEDURE BRINEPROP_SELECT(Conc,Fl$:Fl_brine) holding the
       22 concentration range checks and the 11-branch fluid ladder, rewritten
       as sequential single-line IF statements with mutually exclusive
       conditions (same behaviour);
     - the property evaluation FLATTENED into the main program (library
       decision D10 style) for the two properties this model uses:
         CALL BRINEPROP('Density','PG',conc_glw,t_glw_su_ev:rho_glw_su_ev)
           -> block tagged _rho (Pr = 2: Density as in the original, Fl = 2: PG)
         CALL BRINEPROP('specheat','PG',conc_glw,t_glw_su_ev:cp_glw/1000)
           -> block tagged _cp  (Pr = 3: SpecHeat, Fl = 2: PG)
       The REPEAT loop of the procedure is expanded into its 18 explicit
       equations (CoolSolve counts a DUPLICATE loop counter as an unknown
       without an equation).  The 18-term polynomial, the tables ('Brine1',
       'Brine2'), the row index
       Row[k] = k + (Fl-1)*18 and the output scaling (output = Funkt for
       Density, output = Funkt/1000 for SpecHeat) are kept exactly as in the
       original; the procedure-internal variables are renamed per call
       (<variable>_rho, <variable>_cp).
  2. The expression output of the second call (:cp_glw/1000) becomes the
     equation cp_glw = Funkt_cp: the procedure output of Pr=3 is Funkt/1000, so
     the two factors of 1000 cancel and cp_glw keeps the value of the original
     (3973.6 J/kg-K for this operating point).

  CoolSolve cannot solve the redundant equations of the original (four
  variables are defined twice: h_ex1_cp, M_dot_s_cp, Q_dot_ev and Q_dot_cd -
  the RefSim models compute each quantity from two independent routes, as a
  consistency check), so the four duplicate definitions are turned into
  post-processing CHECKS here (same right-hand sides, new names, no effect on
  the other results):

     h_ex1_cp_chk      = h_thr_cp+1/2*C_thr_cp^2
     M_dot_s_cp_chk    = V_dot_s_cp/v_su2_cp
     Q_dot_ev_chk      = epsilon_ev*C_dot_glw_ev*(t_glw_su_ev-t_ev)
     Q_dot_cd_chk      = epsilon_cd*C_dot_w_cd*(t_cd-t_w_su_cd)
     Q_dot_ev_chk_brine = C_dot_glw_ev*(t_glw_su_ev-t_glw_ex_ev)
     Q_dot_cd_chk_water = C_dot_w_cd*(t_w_ex_cd-t_w_su_cd)
  and the two heat rates are computed from their own side only, the exit
  temperatures t_glw_ex_ev and t_w_ex_cd being given by the explicit
  temperature-rise equations of the original.

  Everything else - variable names, equations, defaults, units - is as in the
  native file. The companion tables of this variant
  (brine_to_water_heat_pump_refsim_coolsolve-Brine1/Brine2.csv) hold the same
  decoded values as the native ones.
=============================================================================}


{Selector part of BRINEPROP: range checks and fluid number (no lookup here,
 so it stays a procedure; the ELSE IF ladders are rewritten as sequential
 single-line IF statements with mutually exclusive conditions)}

Procedure BRINEPROP_SELECT(Conc,Fl$:Fl_brine)

IF (Fl$='EG') AND (Conc<0) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal to or larger than 0.0%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='EG') AND (Conc>56.1) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal to or smaller than 56.1%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='PG') AND (Conc<15.2) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal to or larger than 15.2%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='PG') AND (Conc>57.0) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal to or smaller than 57.0%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='EA') AND (Conc<11.1) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal to or larger than 11.1%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='EA') AND (Conc>60.1) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal or smaller than 60.1%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='MA') AND (Conc<7.8) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal to or larger than 7.8%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='MA') AND (Conc>44.3) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal or smaller than 44.3%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='GL') AND (Conc<19.5) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal to or larger than 19.5%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='GL') AND (Conc>63.0) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal or smaller than 63.0%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='NH3') AND (Conc<7.8) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal to or larger than 7.8%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='NH3') AND (Conc>23.6) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal to or smaller than 23.6%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='K2CO3') AND (Conc<13.3) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal to or larger than 13.3%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='K2CO3') AND (Conc>39.0) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal to or smaller than 39.0%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='CaCl2') AND (Conc<9.0) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal to or larger than 9.0%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='CaCl2') AND (Conc>29.4) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal or smaller than 29.4%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='MgCl2') AND (Conc<7.2) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal to or larger than 7.2%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='MgCl2') AND (Conc>20.5) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal or smaller than 20.5%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='NaCl') AND (Conc<7.9) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal to or larger than 7.9%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='NaCl') AND (Conc>22.6) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal to or smaller than 22.6%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='KAc') AND (Conc<11.0) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal to or larger than 11.0%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)
IF (Fl$='KAc') AND (Conc>41.0) THEN Call ERROR('Concentration must be equal to or smaller than 41.0%. Try setting the lower limit in the Variables Info window according to the values indicated in the help file.',Conc)

"Fluid parameter of the original ELSE IF ladder, as sequential IF statements"
EG=1;PG=2;EA=3;MA=4;GL=5;NH3=6;K2CO3=7;CaCl2=8;MgCl2=9;NaCl=10;KAc=11
Fl_brine=0
IF (Fl$='EG') THEN Fl_brine:=EG
IF (Fl$='PG') THEN Fl_brine:=PG
IF (Fl$='EA') THEN Fl_brine:=EA
IF (Fl$='MA') THEN Fl_brine:=MA
IF (Fl$='GL') THEN Fl_brine:=GL
IF (Fl$='NH3') THEN Fl_brine:=NH3
IF (Fl$='K2CO3') THEN Fl_brine:=K2CO3
IF (Fl$='CaCl2') THEN Fl_brine:=CaCl2
IF (Fl$='MgCl2') THEN Fl_brine:=MgCl2
IF (Fl$='NaCl') THEN Fl_brine:=NaCl
IF (Fl$='KAc') THEN Fl_brine:=KAc
IF (Fl_brine=0) THEN Call ERROR('Unrecognized fluid name: the BrineProp library knows EG, PG, EA, MA, GL, NH3, K2CO3, CaCl2, MgCl2, NaCl and KAc.')
END

"{--- end of the selector procedure ---}"

CALL BRINEPROP_SELECT(conc_glw,'PG':Fl_brine)

"!title: BRINE TO WATER HEAT PUMP"

"Date : 2008 January 8"
"Authors: Vincent Lemort"
"University of Liège"
"Faculty of Applied Sciences"
"Thermodynamics Laboratory"
"!Short description:"
"This model describes a brine to water heat pump. The model includes a scroll compressor model, a brine evaporator model and a water condenser model."

"!Nomenclature (as in the original):"
"A            Area [m^2]"
"AU           Global heat transfer coefficient [W/K]"
"C            Velocity [m/s]"
"conc         Concentration [%]"
"COP          Coefficient of performance [-]"
"c_p          Specific heat [J/kg-K]"
"h            Specific enthalpy [J/kg]"
"M_dot        Mass flow rate [kg/s]"
"NtU          Number of transfer units [-]"
"p            Pressure [Pa]"
"Q_dot        Thermal power [W]"
"R            Thermal resistance [K/W]"
"r_p          Pressure ratio [-]"
"r_v_in       Internal built-in volume ratio [-]"
"s            Specific entropy [J/kg-K]"
"t            Temperature [C]"
"v            Specific volume [m^3/kg]"
"V_dot_s      Swept volume [m^3/s]"
"W_dot        Electrical power [W]"
"X            Fraction [-]"
"x            Quality [-]"
"delta_T      Temperature difference [K]"
"epsilon      Efficiency [-]"
"gamma        Isentropic coefficient [-]"
"rho          Density [kg/m^3]"
"Subscripts: amb (ambient), cd (condenser), cp (compressor), ev (evaporator),"
" ex (exhaust), glw (glycol water, brine), leak (leakage), loss (mechanical"
" losses), n (nominal), oh (overheating), r (refrigerant), s (isentropic),"
" sc (subcooling), su (supply), thr (throat), w (water, envelope)"

"!Reference:"
"[1] Winandy, E., C., Saavedra O., J., Lebrun (2002) Experimental analysis and simplified modelling of a hermetic scroll refrigeration compressor. Applied thermal Engineering 22, 107-120."

"!Disclaimer of the original: the accuracy or reliability of the information is not guaranteed; the model is freely distributed and may not be sold; the user is asked to cite his sources and the origin of the model."

"!*************************************************** MODEL ***************************************************"

"!1. INPUTS (panel of the original; the values below are those of the run whose solution is stored in the file, see the README conversion log)"
t_amb=25                               "ambient temperature [C]"
fluid$='R407C'                         "refrigerant [-]"
n_cp=1                                 "number of compressors [-]"
t_w_su_cd=25.50380279                  "water supply temperature at the condenser [C]"
p_w_su_cd=400000                       "water supply pressure at the condenser [Pa]"
t_glw_su_ev=0                          "brine supply temperature at the evaporator [C]"
DELTAt_oh_ev=5                         "superheating at the evaporator exhaust [K]"
DELTAt_sc_cd=5                         "subcooling at the condenser exhaust [K]"
M_dot_w_cd=0.3889                      "water flow rate at the condenser [kg/s]"
M_dot_glw_ev=1.11                      "brine flow rate at the evaporator [kg/s]"
X_cp=1                                 "fraction of the swept volume in use [-]"
conc_glw=25                            "glycol concentration of the brine [%]"
P_ev=436182.6219                       "evaporating pressure [Pa]"
P_cd=1730328.509                       "condensing pressure [Pa]"
M_dot_r=0.07561309079                  "refrigerant mass flow rate through the compressor [kg/s]"

"!2. PARAMETERS (panel of the original; the values below are those of the stored run)"
"!2.1. Compressor"
A_leak_cp=5e-07                        "leakage area of the scroll throat [m^2]"
r_v_in_cp=3.2                          "internal built-in volume ratio [-]"
W_dot_loss0_cp=150                    "constant electro-mechanical losses [W]"
alpha_cp=0.25                          "loss factor proportional to the internal power [-]"
M_dot_r_cp_n=0.12                      "nominal refrigerant mass flow rate [kg/s]"
N_rot=3000                             "rotation speed [tr/min]"
AU_su_cp_n=25                          "nominal heat transfer coefficient at the compressor supply [W/K]"
AU_amb_cp=10                           "heat transfer coefficient compressor-ambient [W/K]"
AU_ex_cp_n=30                          "nominal heat transfer coefficient at the compressor exhaust [W/K]"
V_s_cp_ref=9.477777778e-05             "reference swept volume of the compressor [m^3]"

"!2.2. Brine evaporator"
R_m_ev=1e-05                           "metal resistance of the evaporator [K/W]"
R_glw_ev_n=6e-05                       "nominal brine-side resistance [K/W]"
R_r_ev_n=6e-05                         "nominal refrigerant-side resistance [K/W]"
M_dot_glw_ev_n=1.121                   "nominal brine flow rate [kg/s]"
M_dot_r_ev_n=0.12                      "nominal refrigerant flow rate [kg/s]"

"!2.3. Water condenser"
M_dot_w_cd_n=0.389                     "nominal water flow rate [kg/s]"
R_m_cd=1e-05                           "metal resistance of the condenser [K/W]"
R_w_cd_n=0.0003                        "nominal water-side resistance [K/W]"
R_r_cd_n=0.0003                        "nominal refrigerant-side resistance [K/W]"
M_dot_r_cd_n=0.12                      "nominal refrigerant flow rate [kg/s]"

"!3. OUTPUTS"
"delta_T [C]: temperature variation; y [W]: power"

"!4. EQUATIONS"
"!4.1. Scroll compressor [1]"
"4.1.1. Status supply: su"
DELTAt_oh_su_cp=DELTAt_oh_ev                                    "superheating of the supply gas [K]"
t_sat_su_cp=temperature(fluid$,P=P_ev,x=1)                      "saturation temperature at the supply pressure [C]"
t_su_cp=t_sat_su_cp+DELTAt_oh_su_cp                              "supply temperature [C]"
P_su_cp=P_ev                                                    "supply pressure [Pa]"
h_su_cp=enthalpy(fluid$,t=t_su_cp,P=P_su_cp)                    "specific enthalpy [J/kg]"
s_su_cp=entropy(fluid$,t=t_su_cp,P=P_su_cp)                     "specific entropy [J/kg-K]"
v_su_cp=volume(fluid$,t=t_su_cp,P=P_su_cp)                      "specific volume [m^3/kg]"

"4.1.2. Heating-up: su => su1"
c_p_su_cp = specheat(fluid$,t=t_su_cp,P=P_su_cp)                "specific heat of the supply gas [J/kg-K]"
C_dot_su_cp = M_dot_r*c_p_su_cp                                  "capacity flow rate of the supply gas [W/K]"
AU_su_cp=AU_su_cp_n*(M_dot_r/M_dot_r_cp_n)^0.8                  "conductance at the supply [W/K]"
NtU_su_cp = AU_su_cp/C_dot_su_cp                                "number of transfer units [-]"
epsilon_su_cp = 1-exp(-NtU_su_cp)                                "effectiveness [-]"
Q_dot_su_cp = epsilon_su_cp*C_dot_su_cp*(t_w_cp-t_su_cp)        "heat transfer to the supply gas [W]"
h_su1_cp = h_su_cp+Q_dot_su_cp/M_dot_r                          "specific enthalpy after heating-up [J/kg]"
p_su1_cp=p_su_cp                                                 "no pressure drop, as in the original [Pa]"
t_su1_cp = temperature(fluid$,h=h_su1_cp,p=p_su1_cp)            "temperature after heating-up [C]"
DELTAt_su_cp=t_su1_cp-t_su_cp                                    "temperature rise [K]"
v_su1_cp = volume(fluid$,t=t_su1_cp,p=p_su1_cp)                 "specific volume [m^3/kg]"
s_su1_cp= entropy(fluid$,t=t_su1_cp,p=p_su1_cp)                  "specific entropy [J/kg-K]"

"4.1.3. Mixing with internal leakage: su1 => su2"
M_dot_s_cp=M_dot_r+M_dot_leak_cp                                 "mass flow rate entering the compression chamber [kg/s]"
h_su2_cp=(M_dot_r*h_su1_cp+M_dot_leak_cp*h_ex1_cp)/M_dot_s_cp          "mixing of the two streams; the mixing equation of the original 4.1.3 written explicitly on h_su2_cp [J/kg]"

"4.1.4. Flow rate calculation: su2"
M_dot_s_cp_chk=V_dot_s_cp/v_su2_cp                                "check: mass flow rate from the swept volume (original 4.1.4) [kg/s]"
v_su2_cp=volume(fluid$,P=P_su_cp,h=h_su2_cp)                     "specific volume entering the compression chamber [m^3/kg]"
s_su2_cp=entropy(fluid$,P=P_su_cp,h=h_su2_cp)                    "specific entropy entering the compression chamber [J/kg-K]"
V_dot_s_cp_max=V_s_cp_ref*(N_rot/60)                             "maximum swept volume flow rate [m^3/s]"
V_dot_s_cp=V_dot_s_cp_max*X_cp                                    "swept volume flow rate [m^3/s]"
V_dot_s_cp_m3h=V_dot_s_cp*3600                                   "swept volume flow rate [m^3/h]"

"4.1.5. Isentropic compression from the supply pressure up to the adapted pressure: su2 => in"
"The first compression is adiabatic-reversible and so isentropic, up to the adapted pressure."
s_in_cp=s_su2_cp                                                "isentropic compression [J/kg-K]"
v_in_cp=v_su2_cp/r_v_in_cp                                       "definition of the internal built-in volume ratio [m^3/kg]"
t_in_cp = temperature(fluid$,P=p_in_cp,s=s_in_cp)               "temperature at the adapted pressure, added for the (P, s) pair below [C]"
h_in_cp = enthalpy(fluid$,P=p_in_cp,s=s_in_cp)                  "specific enthalpy at the adapted pressure (decision D11: the original wrote the pair (s, v)) [J/kg]"
w_in1_cp= h_in_cp-h_su2_cp                                       "isentropic compression work [J/kg]"
p_in_cp=pressure(fluid$,T=t_in_cp,v=v_in_cp)                     "adapted pressure (decision D11: the original wrote the pair (s, v)) [Pa]"

"4.1.6. Isochoric compression from the adapted pressure up to the exhaust pressure: in => ex1"
"The second compression is also adiabatic, but not reversible and at constant absolute volume (this second part corresponds to the opening of the compression chamber to the discharge plenum)."
p_ex1_cp=p_ex_cp                                                 "no pressure drop [Pa]"
p_ex_cp=P_cd                                                     "exhaust pressure [Pa]"
w_in2_cp= v_in_cp*(p_ex1_cp-p_in_cp)                             "isochoric compression work [J/kg]"

"4.1.7. Total compression work and power"
w_in_cp=w_in1_cp+w_in2_cp                                        "total compression work [J/kg]"
W_dot_in_cp=M_dot_r*w_in_cp                                      "internal power of the compressor [W]"
h_ex1_cp=h_su2_cp+w_in_cp                                        "both compression steps are considered adiabatic, from su2 to ex1 [J/kg]"
v_ex1_cp=volume(fluid$,P=P_ex1_cp,h=h_ex1_cp)                    "specific volume at the compressor exhaust [m^3/kg]"

"4.1.8. Electrical consumption"
W_dot_cp=W_dot_in_cp+W_dot_loss_cp                               "the compressor electrical power is split into two terms [W]"
W_dot_loss_cp=W_dot_loss0_cp+alpha_cp*W_dot_in_cp                "constant electro-mechanical losses + losses proportional to the internal power [W]"

"4.1.9. Internal leakage: ex1 => su1"
s_ex1_cp=entropy(fluid$,P=P_ex1_cp,h=h_ex1_cp)                   "specific entropy at the compressor exhaust [J/kg-K]"
s_thr_cp=s_ex1_cp                                                "isentropic flow to the throat [J/kg-K]"
C_thr_cp^2=2*(h_ex1_cp-h_thr_cp)                                         "leakage velocity at the throat, from the energy relation h_ex1_cp=h_thr_cp+1/2*C_thr_cp^2 of the original [m^2/s^2]"
V_dot_leak_cp=A_leak_cp*C_thr_cp                                      "leakage volume flow rate [m^3/s]"
h_ex1_cp_chk=h_thr_cp+1/2*C_thr_cp^2                              "check: conservation of the total enthalpy in the leakage orifice (original 4.1.9) [J/kg]"
h_thr_cp=enthalpy(fluid$,P=P_thr_cp,s=s_thr_cp)                  "specific enthalpy at the throat [J/kg]"
M_dot_leak_cp=V_dot_leak_cp/v_thr_cp                             "leakage mass flow rate [kg/s]"
v_thr_cp=volume(fluid$,P=P_thr_cp,s=s_thr_cp)                    "specific volume at the throat [m^3/kg]"
P_thr_cp=max(P_thr_crit,P_su1_cp)                                "throat pressure [Pa]"
P_thr_crit=P_ex1_cp*(2/(gamma_leak_cp+1))^(gamma_leak_cp/(gamma_leak_cp-1))  "critical pressure of the leakage flow [Pa]"
gamma_leak_cp=1.03                                                      "isentropic coefficient of the leakage flow; the original leaves it commented out (this default value) and lets the leakage relations solve it (see the README)"
P_thr_chk=P_ex1_cp*(v_ex1_cp/v_thr_cp)^gamma_leak_cp    "check: isentropic relation across the leakage orifice, P_thr_cp = P_ex1_cp*(v_ex1_cp/v_thr_cp)^gamma_leak_cp is the original equation P_ex1_cp*v_ex1_cp^gamma_leak_cp = P_thr_cp*v_thr_cp^gamma_leak_cp [Pa]"

"4.1.10. Exhaust cooling-down: ex1 => ex"
t_ex1_cp=temperature(fluid$,h=h_ex1_cp,p=p_ex1_cp)               "temperature at the compressor exhaust [C]"
AU_ex_cp=AU_ex_cp_n*(M_dot_r/M_dot_r_cp_n)^0.8                    "conductance at the exhaust [W/K]"
c_p_ex1_cp = specheat(fluid$,t=t_ex1_cp,P=p_ex1_cp)              "specific heat of the discharge gas [J/kg-K]"
C_dot_ex_cp = M_dot_r*c_p_ex1_cp                                 "capacity flow rate of the discharge gas [W/K]"
NtU_ex_cp = AU_ex_cp/C_dot_ex_cp                                 "number of transfer units [-]"
epsilon_ex_cp = 1-exp(-NtU_ex_cp)                                "effectiveness [-]"
Q_dot_ex_cp = epsilon_ex_cp*C_dot_ex_cp*(t_w_cp-t_ex1_cp)        "heat transfer from the discharge gas [W]"
h_ex_cp  = h_ex1_cp+Q_dot_ex_cp/M_dot_r                          "specific enthalpy at the compressor exhaust [J/kg]"
t_ex_cp=temperature(fluid$,h=h_ex_cp,p=p_ex_cp)                  "compressor exhaust temperature [C]"
DELTAt_ex_cp=t_ex_cp-t_ex1_cp                                    "temperature drop [K]"

"4.1.11. Fictitious envelope heat balance"
t_w_cp=t_amb+(W_dot_loss_cp-Q_dot_su_cp-Q_dot_ex_cp)/AU_amb_cp         "fictitious envelope temperature; the heat balance of the original 4.1.11, 0 = W_dot_loss_cp-Q_dot_su_cp-Q_dot_ex_cp-Q_dot_amb_cp, written explicitly on t_w_cp [C]"
Q_dot_amb_cp = AU_amb_cp*(t_w_cp-t_amb)                          "heat exchange with the ambient [W]"

"4.1.12. Volumetric effectiveness"
epsilon_v_cp=v_su_cp/v_su1_cp                                    "volumetric effectiveness [-]"

"4.1.13. Global isentropic effectiveness"
h_exs_cp = enthalpy(fluid$,p=p_ex_cp,s=s_su_cp)                  "specific enthalpy of the isentropic compression [J/kg]"
w_s_cp=h_exs_cp-h_su_cp                                          "isentropic compression work [J/kg]"
w_cp=W_dot_cp/M_dot_r                                            "specific electrical power [J/kg]"
epsilon_s_cp= w_s_cp/w_cp                                        "global isentropic effectiveness [-]"

"4.1.14. Pressure ratio"
r_p_cp=P_ex_cp/P_su_cp                                           "pressure ratio [-]"

"!4.2. Brine evaporator"
"4.2.1. Effectiveness"
NtU_ev=AU_ev/C_dot_glw_ev                                        "number of transfer units [-]"
epsilon_ev=1-exp(-NtU_ev)                                        "effectiveness [-]"
AU_ev=1/(R_glw_ev+R_m_ev+R_r_ev)                                   "three thermal resistances in series, 1/AU_ev = R_glw_ev+R_m_ev+R_r_ev as in the original [W/K]"
R_glw_ev=R_glw_ev_n*(M_dot_glw_ev_n/M_dot_glw_ev)^0.8             "brine-side resistance [K/W]"
R_r_ev=R_r_ev_n*(M_dot_r_ev_n/M_dot_r_ev)^0.8                    "refrigerant-side resistance [K/W]"

"4.2.2. Evaporating power"
Q_dot_ev_chk=epsilon_ev*C_dot_glw_ev*(t_glw_su_ev-t_ev)          "check: evaporating power from the effectiveness (original 4.2.2) [W]"

"4.2.3. Refrigerant side"
M_dot_r_ev=n_cp*M_dot_r                                          "refrigerant flow rate [kg/s]"
h_su_ev=h_ex_cd                                                  "isenthalpic expansion [J/kg]"
h_ex_ev=h_su_cp                                                  "refrigerant enters the compressor [J/kg]"
t_sat_ex_ev=temperature(fluid$,P=P_ev,x=1)                       "saturation temperature at the evaporating pressure [C]"
t_su_ev=temperature(fluid$,P=P_ev,h=h_su_ev)                     "temperature after the expansion valve [C]"
t_ev=(t_sat_ex_ev+t_su_ev)/2                                     "mean evaporating temperature [C]"
Q_dot_ev=M_dot_r_ev*(h_ex_ev-h_su_ev)                            "evaporating power, refrigerant side [W]"

"4.2.4. Brine side"
V_dot_glw_min_ev=3900E-3/3600                                    "minimum brine volume flow rate [m^3/s]"
M_dot_glw_min_ev=V_dot_glw_min_ev*rho_glw_su_ev                   "minimum brine mass flow rate [kg/s]"
{--- BRINEPROP('Density','PG',conc_glw,t_glw_su_ev), flattened into the main
     program (see the header): the procedure-internal variables of the original
     are renamed with the suffix _rho. The polynomial, the tables, the row
     index and the output scaling are those of the BrineProp library. ---}
Pr_rho=2
Row_rho[1]=1+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[1]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[1],Pr_rho)
Row_rho[2]=2+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[2]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[2],Pr_rho)
Row_rho[3]=3+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[3]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[3],Pr_rho)
Row_rho[4]=4+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[4]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[4],Pr_rho)
Row_rho[5]=5+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[5]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[5],Pr_rho)
Row_rho[6]=6+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[6]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[6],Pr_rho)
Row_rho[7]=7+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[7]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[7],Pr_rho)
Row_rho[8]=8+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[8]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[8],Pr_rho)
Row_rho[9]=9+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[9]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[9],Pr_rho)
Row_rho[10]=10+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[10]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[10],Pr_rho)
Row_rho[11]=11+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[11]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[11],Pr_rho)
Row_rho[12]=12+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[12]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[12],Pr_rho)
Row_rho[13]=13+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[13]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[13],Pr_rho)
Row_rho[14]=14+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[14]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[14],Pr_rho)
Row_rho[15]=15+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[15]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[15],Pr_rho)
Row_rho[16]=16+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[16]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[16],Pr_rho)
Row_rho[17]=17+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[17]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[17],Pr_rho)
Row_rho[18]=18+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_rho[18]=lookup('Brine1',Row_rho[18],Pr_rho)
xm_rho=lookup('Brine2',Fl_brine,1)
ym_rho=lookup('Brine2',Fl_brine,2)
x_rho=conc_glw-xm_rho
y_rho=t_glw_su_ev-ym_rho
Funkt_rho=c_rho[1]+(c_rho[2]*y_rho)+(c_rho[3]*y_rho^2)+(c_rho[4]*y_rho^3)+(c_rho[5]*x_rho)+(c_rho[6]*x_rho*y_rho)+(c_rho[7]*x_rho*y_rho^2)+(c_rho[8]*x_rho*y_rho^3)+(c_rho[9]*x_rho^2)+(c_rho[10]*x_rho^2*y_rho)+(c_rho[11]*x_rho^2*y_rho^2)+(c_rho[12]*x_rho^2*y_rho^3)+(c_rho[13]*x_rho^3)+(c_rho[14]*x_rho^3*y_rho)+(c_rho[15]*x_rho^3*y_rho^2)+(c_rho[16]*x_rho^4)+(c_rho[17]*x_rho^4*y_rho)+(c_rho[18]*x_rho^5)

{--- end of the Density call ---}
rho_glw_su_ev=Funkt_rho                                              "brine density; output scaling of the original (Pr=2: output=Funkt) [kg/m^3]"
{--- BRINEPROP('specheat','PG',conc_glw,t_glw_su_ev), flattened into the main
     program (see the header): the procedure-internal variables of the original
     are renamed with the suffix _cp. The polynomial, the tables, the row
     index and the output scaling are those of the BrineProp library. ---}
Pr_cp=3
Row_cp[1]=1+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[1]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[1],Pr_cp)
Row_cp[2]=2+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[2]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[2],Pr_cp)
Row_cp[3]=3+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[3]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[3],Pr_cp)
Row_cp[4]=4+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[4]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[4],Pr_cp)
Row_cp[5]=5+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[5]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[5],Pr_cp)
Row_cp[6]=6+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[6]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[6],Pr_cp)
Row_cp[7]=7+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[7]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[7],Pr_cp)
Row_cp[8]=8+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[8]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[8],Pr_cp)
Row_cp[9]=9+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[9]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[9],Pr_cp)
Row_cp[10]=10+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[10]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[10],Pr_cp)
Row_cp[11]=11+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[11]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[11],Pr_cp)
Row_cp[12]=12+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[12]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[12],Pr_cp)
Row_cp[13]=13+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[13]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[13],Pr_cp)
Row_cp[14]=14+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[14]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[14],Pr_cp)
Row_cp[15]=15+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[15]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[15],Pr_cp)
Row_cp[16]=16+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[16]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[16],Pr_cp)
Row_cp[17]=17+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[17]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[17],Pr_cp)
Row_cp[18]=18+(Fl_brine-1)*18
c_cp[18]=lookup('Brine1',Row_cp[18],Pr_cp)
xm_cp=lookup('Brine2',Fl_brine,1)
ym_cp=lookup('Brine2',Fl_brine,2)
xc_cp=conc_glw-xm_cp
yc_cp=t_glw_su_ev-ym_cp
Funkt_cp=c_cp[1]+(c_cp[2]*yc_cp)+(c_cp[3]*yc_cp^2)+(c_cp[4]*yc_cp^3)+(c_cp[5]*xc_cp)+(c_cp[6]*xc_cp*yc_cp)+(c_cp[7]*xc_cp*yc_cp^2)+(c_cp[8]*xc_cp*yc_cp^3)+(c_cp[9]*xc_cp^2)+(c_cp[10]*xc_cp^2*yc_cp)+(c_cp[11]*xc_cp^2*yc_cp^2)+(c_cp[12]*xc_cp^2*yc_cp^3)+(c_cp[13]*xc_cp^3)+(c_cp[14]*xc_cp^3*yc_cp)+(c_cp[15]*xc_cp^3*yc_cp^2)+(c_cp[16]*xc_cp^4)+(c_cp[17]*xc_cp^4*yc_cp)+(c_cp[18]*xc_cp^5)

{--- end of the specheat call ---}
"output scaling of the original for Pr=3: output=Funkt/1000 [kJ/kg-K]"
cp_glw=Funkt_cp                                                      "brine specific heat [J/kg-K] (the procedure output of Pr=3 is Funkt/1000; the original passed the expression cp_glw/1000 as CALL output, so cp_glw = Funkt_cp)"
C_dot_glw_ev=M_dot_glw_ev*cp_glw                                 "brine capacity flow rate [W/K]"
t_glw_ex_ev=t_glw_su_ev-Q_dot_ev/C_dot_glw_ev                       "brine temperature at the evaporator exhaust [C]"
Q_dot_ev_chk_brine=C_dot_glw_ev*(t_glw_su_ev-t_glw_ex_ev)           "check: evaporating power from the brine temperature rise (original 4.2.4) [W]"

"!4.3. Water condenser"
"4.3.1. Effectiveness"
AU_cd=1/(R_w_cd+R_m_cd+R_r_cd)                                     "three thermal resistances in series, 1/AU_cd = R_w_cd+R_m_cd+R_r_cd as in the original [W/K]"
R_w_cd=R_w_cd_n*(M_dot_w_cd_n/M_dot_w_cd)^0.8                    "water-side resistance [K/W]"
R_r_cd=R_r_cd_n*(M_dot_r_cd_n/M_dot_r_cd)^0.8                    "refrigerant-side resistance [K/W]"
NtU_cd=AU_cd/C_dot_w_cd                                          "number of transfer units [-]"
epsilon_cd=1-exp(-NtU_cd)                                        "effectiveness [-]"

"4.3.2. Condensing power"
Q_dot_cd_chk=epsilon_cd*C_dot_w_cd*(t_cd-t_w_su_cd)               "check: condensing power from the effectiveness (original 4.3.2) [W]"

"4.3.3. Refrigerant side"
DELTAt_oh_su_cd=t_ex_cp-t_sat_su_cd                              "superheating at the compressor exhaust [K]"
t_sat_su_cd=temperature(fluid$,P=P_cd,x=1)                       "saturation temperature at the condensing pressure [C]"
t_sat_ex_cd=temperature(fluid$,P=P_cd,x=0)                       "saturation temperature at the condensing pressure [C]"
t_cd=(t_sat_su_cd+t_sat_ex_cd)/2                                 "mean condensing temperature [C]"
M_dot_r_cd=n_cp*M_dot_r                                          "refrigerant flow rate [kg/s]"
h_su_cd=h_ex_cp                                                  "refrigerant enters the condenser [J/kg]"
t_ex_cd=t_sat_ex_cd-DELTAt_sc_cd                                 "temperature at the condenser exhaust [C]"
h_ex_cd=enthalpy(fluid$,t=t_ex_cd,p=P_cd)                        "specific enthalpy at the condenser exhaust [J/kg]"
Q_dot_cd=M_dot_r_cd*(h_su_cd-h_ex_cd)                            "condensing power, refrigerant side [W]"

"4.3.4. Water side"
V_dot_w_min_cd=1400E-3/3600                                      "minimum water volume flow rate [m^3/s]"
M_dot_w_min_cd=V_dot_w_min_cd*rho_w_su_cd                         "minimum water mass flow rate [kg/s]"
rho_w_su_cd=density(water,P=P_w_su_cd,t=t_w_su_cd)               "water density [kg/m^3]"
cp_w=4187                                                        "specific heat of the water [J/kg-K]"
C_dot_w_cd=M_dot_w_cd*cp_w                                       "water capacity flow rate [W/K]"
t_w_ex_cd=t_w_su_cd+Q_dot_cd/C_dot_w_cd                              "water temperature at the condenser exhaust [C]"
Q_dot_cd_chk_water=C_dot_w_cd*(t_w_ex_cd-t_w_su_cd)                  "check: condensing power from the water temperature rise (original 4.3.4) [W]"

"!4.4. Performances of the system"
W_dot_cp_tot=n_cp*W_dot_cp                                       "total electrical power of the compressors [W]"
COP_heating=Q_dot_cd/W_dot_cp_tot                                "heating COP of the system [-]"

"!5. State points for the thermodynamic diagrams (CoolSolve *Diagram* tab, *Array overlay*)"
"i = 1 evaporator exhaust (compressor supply), 2 compressor exhaust (condenser supply), 3 condenser exhaust (expansion valve supply), 4 evaporator supply."
P[1]=P_ev                                    "state 1 pressure [Pa]"
h[1]=h_ex_ev                                 "state 1 enthalpy [J/kg]"
T[1]=t_su_cp                                 "state 1 temperature [C]"
s[1]=s_su_cp                                 "state 1 entropy [J/kg-K]"
P[2]=P_cd                                    "state 2 pressure [Pa]"
h[2]=h_ex_cp                                 "state 2 enthalpy [J/kg]"
T[2]=t_ex_cp                                 "state 2 temperature [C]"
s[2]=entropy(fluid$,P=P_cd,h=h_ex_cp)        "state 2 entropy [J/kg-K]"
P[3]=P_cd                                    "state 3 pressure [Pa]"
h[3]=h_ex_cd                                 "state 3 enthalpy [J/kg]"
T[3]=t_ex_cd                                 "state 3 temperature [C]"
s[3]=entropy(fluid$,P=P_cd,h=h_ex_cd)        "state 3 entropy [J/kg-K]"
P[4]=P_ev                                    "state 4 pressure [Pa]"
h[4]=h_su_ev                                 "state 4 enthalpy [J/kg]"
T[4]=t_su_ev                                 "state 4 temperature [C]"
s[4]=entropy(fluid$,P=P_ev,h=h_su_ev)        "state 4 entropy (two-phase state) [J/kg-K]"
